  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed with the particle に to indicate which club one joins: ～{部|ぶ}に{入部|にゅうぶ}する. Primarily a school context word. The opposite is {退部|たいぶ}する (to quit a club).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ～{部|ぶ}に{入部|にゅうぶ}する (to join ~ club)\n- {入部届|にゅうぶとどけ} (club membership application form)\n- {入部|にゅうぶ}{希望|きぼう} (wish to join a club)\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nIn Japanese schools, joining a club ({部活|ぶかつ}) is considered an important part of education. Many students join in April at the start of the school year after attending trial sessions ({体験入部|たいけんにゅうぶ}).",
